# `Object.create(holder.above)`: nothing is proven of the operand. The code in line looks at it itself: below null and below an object it makes the object, and whatever else comes it leaves to the function,
# which stands behind its miss and refuses the operand in its own words.
# function below(above) { return Object.create(above); }
